course: dictionary
lesson: 9699
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the author means. Read the words around the word. «Each politician picked the part that suited them.» Here suited means fitted or was right for them, not a set of clothes.
explain: Suit can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). As a noun, a suit is a set of clothes or special clothing for one job. As a verb, to suit means to look good on someone, or to be right for them. «Different languages suit different jobs» means each language is right for certain jobs.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it in. Does «Monday suits me» still make sense if you say «Monday is right for me»? Yes, so that is the right meaning. If the sentence stops making sense, try another meaning until it fits.
fact: Suit can be a noun or a verb.
fact: A suit is a set of clothes made of the same cloth, usually a jacket with trousers or a skirt.
fact: In cards, a suit is one of four sets: hearts, diamonds, clubs and spades. Each suit has 13 cards.
fact: «Suit» as a verb means to look good on someone, or to be right or convenient for them.
fact: «Suited» means fitting or right for something, as in «beaks suited to seeds».
exercise: «Different languages suit different jobs.» What does suit mean here? | Argue about | Are dressed in | Are sold in shops | *Are right for
exercise: A pack of playing cards has four of what? | Courts | *Suits | Jobs | Beaks
exercise: «Blue suits you.» What does suits mean? | Is a set of clothes | *Looks good on | Is short and rude | Is a case brought to court
test: «Monday suits me.» What does suits mean? | Is a card in the pack | Is a set of clothes | *Is right and convenient for me | Is a case in court
test: «Every pet needs company, or the right to live alone if that suits it.» What does suits mean? | Is brought to court | Is a spade in a pack of cards | Is dressed in a jacket and trousers | *Is right for it
exam: «Darwin's finches have beaks suited to seeds, insects or cactus.» What does suited mean? | *Fitting or right for | Brought to court | Dressed in | Sad and gloomy
